    "raw": "Unify the \"operate on all todos\" idiom to ONE form: an `ALL` positional-selector\nsentinel, replacing the `--all` flag on `doctor` and `log`.\n\nWhy (from the 2026-07-25 design discussion):\n- The selector grammar collapses to a single positional slot: self | curr |\n  <id-prefix> | ALL. `doctor ALL`, `log ALL`, and any future sweeper read\n  identically.\n- It mirrors the existing `--states=ALL` uppercase-macro convention already in\n  this codebase (uppercase = \"the whole set\"), so `doctor ALL` echoes\n  `--states=ALL`. One word, one meaning.\n- It drops a special flag instead of adding flag surface, and composes:\n  `search ... --states=ALL` and `doctor ALL` share the word.\n\nScope:\n- Selector resolution recognizes the uppercase sentinel `ALL` as \"every todo in\n  the corpus\" (alongside self/curr and id prefixes). `ALL` is reserved (ids are\n  hex, so no collision).\n- `doctor ALL` replaces `doctor --all` (sweep the whole corpus / audit + repair\n  + schema sweep + auto-tag recompute across all todos).\n- `log ALL` replaces `log --all` (render every root as a forest).\n- Remove the `--all` argparse flag (dest sweep_all) from both commands.\n- Update help strings and SKILL.md (the doctor/log CLI rows + the Selectors\n  section) to document the `ALL` sentinel.\n- Update tests: `doctor --all` -> `doctor ALL`, `log --all` -> `log ALL`; add a\n  case asserting `--all` is no longer accepted.\n\nNon-goals:\n- `ls` / `search` are unchanged -- they are the inherent \"null-query = all\" case\n  and take no selector (consistent with Unix listing norms).\n- No other subcommand gains an ALL mode.\n\nWorking model: worked per skills/projectmanagement/PLAN.md (Opus orchestrator /\nSonnet implementor); the AC is a frozen test."
  },
